  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Corruption remains an everyday occurrence in many Pacific Island Countries (PICs), diverting critical resources from PIC governments&#x2019; budget and undermining efforts to progress people-centred sustainable development. It also risks undermining peace and stability, contributing to lack of trust in government and sometimes leading to the actual undermining of governments. Corruption also makes PICs less safe when it leads to governance weaknesses that enable money-laundering and organised crime to</narrative>
  </description>
